Emulating the Linear/Logarithmic Mode Switch

Later EMS expander iterations added a switch to toggle between Linear and Logarithmic slew response curves.
• Linear Mode: The implementation above represents linear mode. The voltage rises like a straight ramp regardless of how close it is to the target.
• Logarithmic Mode: To emulate this mode, multiply \(\text{MaxChange}\) by a fraction of the absolute remaining difference. This causes the slew rate to start aggressively fast and flatten out exponentially as it approaches the target voltage—perfect for modeling smooth vintage portamento.